{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: stop a hand-appended statement from censoring the connector's genuine GitHub observation. This is the current-world replacement for stale request 895f3126, which you asked me to retire and refile; I am retiring it in the same wave and this request rests on the live internal/connector artifact f23514ba rather than on the 2026-08-11 assessment chain, so nothing here is stale from birth.\n\nI re-verified the defect myself at main 4200aa27 rather than taking the re-verification on trust. internal/connector/github/observe.go:121 Fold walks projected statements and keys a correspondence on exactly two body fields: it skips anything whose body[\"source\"] is not \"github\" (:124) and anything with an empty body[\"external_id\"] (:127), then records the first event that named each external id, first writer wins (:134). Nothing anywhere in that loop asks who wrote the statement, what kind it is, or whether the connector is the author.\n\nWHY THAT MATTERS, stated as the attack rather than as a property. Any participant can append an ordinary statement carrying source github and an external_id that the connector has not yet observed. Fold then treats that external object as already observed, Unobserved drops it, and the connector never emits the real observation. The genuine act is not overwritten — it is never made. First-writer-wins, which is the right rule between a real observation and a later duplicate, becomes the mechanism: the forger only has to be early, and being early is free because external ids are public. The result is a silent hole in what the log says it saw, and the log's whole claim is that what it knew was always in it.\n\nWHAT I AM NOT ASKING FOR. Do not add connector-private state to fix this. The comment above Fold is right that a connector needing private state to be correct has a design problem, and that property is worth more than this defect costs. The fix belongs inside the fold: restrict which statements count as prior observations, using facts the log already carries.\n\nThe obvious restriction is authorship — only statements the connector actor wrote are observations — and I think that is correct, but I am not mandating it, because you are closer to how the connector's identity reaches this package and Fold currently takes a Statement shape carrying only Event and Body. If authorship is not available at this seam without dragging identity into a package that deliberately does no I/O, say so in your artifact and propose what you did instead; the condition is that a non-connector statement cannot suppress a real observation, not that you implement my sketch.\n\nMind the ordering hazard while you are here: whatever you key on, a statement the fold refuses must not silently become an observation later by another route, and a correction genuinely written by the connector must still win over a duplicate the way it does today.","body":{"conditions":"1. A statement not written by the connector cannot enter the correspondence as a prior observation, so it cannot cause Unobserved to drop a real one. 2. An adversarial test appends a statement carrying source github and an unobserved external_id from a non-connector actor and requires the genuine observation still to be emitted; it must fail if the restriction is weakened, verified by making that edit and watching it fail. 3. Existing behaviour preserved: a genuine connector observation still wins over a later duplicate naming the same external id, and the connector still needs no private state — no disk, no cache, no I/O added to this package. 4. If authorship is not reachable at the Fold seam without importing identity into internal/connector/github, say so explicitly in the artifact and state what you keyed on instead and why it is sufficient. 5. make vet, make test, make race, make build, gofmt and diff-check pass at the exact head; artifact at every maintained path the head changes; independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review before merge.","priority":"P2","replaces":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:895f3126e7c6ae524ce4dc62c3e8c65ac770a071","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123","verified_at":"main 4200aa27 on 2026-08-21"}}